# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-lzc.md#decoding-a-code
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0065, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0069, PV-0080, PV-0350, PV-0310, PV-0312, PV-0384, PV-0385, PV-0386, PV-0388, PV-0391, PV-0392, PV-0395, PV-0314
# kind: decompress
# description: ABABABA: the fourth code equals next free, the entry being defined at that moment.
# derivation: Header: length 7, byte 7 0x90. Codes, 9 bits each, LSB first (PV-0388): 0x041 (A; first code, no entry), 0x042 (B; entry 257 = AB), 257 (AB; entry 258 = BA), 259 = next free, so its string is AB + A = ABA and entry 259 = ABA (PV-0386, PV-0391, PV-0392). Bits 0-8 = 0x041, 9-17 = 0x042, 18-26 = 0x101, 27-35 = 0x103, 36-39 zero, giving 41 84 04 1C 08.
# expect.error: none
# expect.algorithm: lzc
# expect.uncompressed_length: 7
# expect.block_mode: 1
# expect.output_length: 7
# expect.output: 41 42 41 42 41 42 41
hex:
07 00 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
11                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
90                                                # byte 7
41 84 04 1C 08                                    # codes 0x041, 0x042, 0x101, 0x103 (9 bits each); 4 spare zero bits
